==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{m|is|hvat}}, originally the neuter form of {{m|non|*hver}} (from {{etyl|gem-pro|is}} {{m|gem-pro|*hwaz}}), but conflated with {{m|non|hverr}} (whence Modern Icelandic {{m|is|hver}}). Corresponds to {{etyl|gem-pro|is}} {{m|gem-pro|*hwat}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|is}} {{m|ine-pro|*kʷód}}, {{m|ine-pro|*kʷod}}. See {{m|is|hver}}.

